What is derived, and how
------------------------

No Simple source is copied into this repository. This project is a **re-implementation in Coil** of
the algorithms Simple demonstrates, for a different language (TypeScript/JavaScript rather than
Simple's C-like language) and on a different runtime. What is taken is the DESIGN: the sea-of-nodes
IR, the structure of its passes, and in many cases the precise sequence of steps within a pass.

`docs/LAYOUT.md` carries the correspondence between this tree and Simple's.

Modifications
-------------

Everything here is modified relative to Simple, in the sense of Apache-2.0 §4(b): it is a
translation into another language, restructured (Simple's ~70 single-class node files are grouped
into ~16 thematic modules here), and extended with machinery Simple does not have — a dynamic value
axis and NaN boxing, hidden classes and shape-based alias classes, guards as control flow, a
GC-abstract IR with safepoints and relocation, exceptions, closures, and the JSL runtime-library
language. `docs/LAYOUT.md` §4 lists the deliberate extensions; they are marked with `✦` in the tree.

Other components
----------------

`jsl/` — the JavaScript runtime library written in JSL — is the work of this project's author and
is not derived from Simple. Its definitions cite ECMA-262 by section and by specification commit in
their own `:spec` annotations.
